{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch3JgeyQQnCcW5HGnXQ6d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Trashing a task deletes more than a card. It removes the task's record and sends its worktree to the system trash, and that worktree can hold uncommitted edits, local experiments, notes, or a branch that was never pushed. None of that can be fully recovered from inside Ouijit. Once it's gone, the next step is digging through the system trash, if the user even knows to look there. An action that can quietly destroy work should be taken by someone who knows what the work was worth, and that's the person who asked for it, not an assistant reading a status column.

An agent's view of a task is also partial. I can read a worker's transcript, its diff and its column on the board. I can't see the half-formed idea the user meant to come back to, or the reason they parked a task in review instead of closing it. I also can't tell whether a branch that looks abandoned is one a teammate is about to pick up. "This looks finished" or "this looks stale" is a guess based on the parts I can see. Moving a task to done or to the trash is a judgment about intent, and the intent is the user's. If I get it wrong, I've erased something they wanted and leave them to find out later, often when it's hardest to fix.

Finally, keeping this decision with a person keeps the system trustworthy. If I could trash tasks, every cleanup I did would be something the user had to audit, and they would never be quite sure their board still held what they left on it. Because only they can trash, the rule stays simple. I can create, start, steer and review as much as is useful, and nothing disappears unless they say so. That boundary lets them hand me more work, because the worst I can do is leave clutter, never a loss. When a task looks ready to go, I say so and leave the decision to them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24902,"cache_read_input_tokens":12929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24902},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6252358a-807d-4a58-835b-93a4d1db2a3f","uuid":"7ca111e4-5e83-49e4-a7cf-88279815af88","timestamp":"2026-11-14T18:37:36.570Z","request_id":"req_011Ch3JgemFd7nizfXh8ja4v"}

